  "about": "One list, two implementations: extension/shared/jobposting.js:idFrom (tests/test_extension.js) and pipeline/joburl.py:generic_id (tests/test_captures.py) must derive the same posting id from each URL, or a manual entry pasted from a page never converges with a capture of it. Shapes are the ones the 24 Sep 2026 survey of 18 ATS vendors measured (docs/career-sites.md 4.2); every tenant is a placeholder. An apply flow's own tail is not the job's id: Oracle's form at `…/job/2087/apply/section/1` is job 2087, not 1 (28 Sep 2026), so the part of the path before `apply`/`application` is searched first and the tail only when it has none, which is where JazzHR's id is (`/apply/<id>/<slug>`). A SuccessFactors id carries its tenant (`company=`) before the requisition, since one host serves many employers; a sign-in page with no requisition keeps the fallback, and a `company` parameter on any other host is not a tenant. The last cases pin the fallback: with no id-shaped part, the whole path PLUS the non-tracking query, so two jobs on one generic page cannot share an id. On an apply flow's address that query leaves out a parameter naming the wizard's step (Phenom's own apply, 2 Oct 2026: `…/apply?jobSeqNo=…&step=N&stepname=…`), since it is the id the answers store is keyed on and a per-step id emptied the store at every Next; off an apply address a `step` parameter stays. A Workday requisition is short letter groups then digits, hyphens allowed (`_PT-JR012345`, 2 Oct 2026, gave a fallback id under the one-group rule), never a slug word (`_engineer-2024`).",
